cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or quote a number measured in it, please cite it as below."
title: "See the drone, then hit it (SpeckLock)"
abstract: >-
  Two halves of one problem. Detection: find a drone that occupies 3-14 pixels in 720p
  video by stabilising and stacking three grayscale moments, so that the static world
  cancels and movers leave colour trails. Measured on real, hand-labelled video: on a
  near-static camera the stack lifts a controlled single-frame AP of 0.159 to 0.895; on two
  benchmarks whose cameras move (ARD-MAV, NPS-Drones) it does not separate from a single
  frame. Pursuit: close on that drone with camera-only proportional-navigation guidance,
  a four-camera 360-degree ring and a mission FSM — measured closed-loop in NVIDIA Isaac
  Sim. There is no flight test in this repository.
type: software
